# 32×32 RISC-V Register File (RTL to GDSII ASIC Implementation)

## Overview

This project implements a **32-bit, 32-entry RISC-V Register File** in Verilog and demonstrates the complete **RTL-to-GDSII ASIC implementation flow** using the open-source Sky130 toolchain.

Unlike a traditional RTL-only project, this design was successfully taken through every major stage of digital ASIC design including synthesis, floorplanning, placement, clock tree synthesis, routing, physical verification, and final GDSII generation.

---

# Project Objectives

- Design a 32×32 Register File in Verilog
- Verify functionality using a custom SystemVerilog testbench
- Synthesize the RTL into Sky130 standard cells
- Implement the complete physical design flow
- Generate a manufacturable GDSII layout
- Pass DRC and LVS verification

---

# Register File Specifications

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|------:|
| Registers | 32 |
| Register Width | 32 bits |
| Storage | 1024 Flip-Flops |
| Read Ports | 2 |
| Write Ports | 1 |
| Write | Synchronous |
| Read | Asynchronous |
| Reset | Active High |
| x0 Register | Hardwired to Zero |

---

# Features

- 32 General Purpose Registers
- Two Independent Read Ports
- One Write Port
- Active High Reset
- x0 Always Reads Zero
- Writes to x0 Ignored
- Fully Verified RTL
- ASIC Ready Design

